[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: AIM High-Level Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DEC-01
TITLE: Label extraction and check
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_decoder_decode shall extract the 8-bit label from bits 0-7 of the input
word and shall set valid=false whenever the label does not equal 0203 octal
(0x83).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DEC-02
TITLE: SDI extraction
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_decoder_decode shall extract SDI from bits 8-9 of the input word.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DEC-03
TITLE: Altitude field extraction
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_decoder_decode shall extract the 18-bit two's-complement BNR altitude
field from bits 10-27, sign-extend it to int32_t, with LSB = 1 ft.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DEC-04
TITLE: SSM mapping
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_decoder_decode shall extract SSM from bits 28-29 and map it to
AIM_SSM_FAILURE_WARNING / AIM_SSM_NO_COMPUTED_DATA / AIM_SSM_FUNCTIONAL_TEST /
AIM_SSM_NORMAL_OPERATION per the standard ARINC 429 BNR SSM encoding
(00/01/10/11).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DEC-05
TITLE: Parity check
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_decoder_decode shall compute odd parity over bits 0-30 and compare it to
bit 31; parity_ok shall be false on mismatch, and valid shall be false
whenever parity_ok is false.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-2

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-DEC-06
TITLE: Validity independent of SSM
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_decoder_decode shall set valid=true only when the label is correct and
parity_ok is true, regardless of SSM value; SSM is reported separately for
use by the alerter and monitor.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-2

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-01
TITLE: Selected altitude hold and range check
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_alerter_update shall hold the last-valid selected altitude across calls
and shall reject (not adopt) a new selected altitude outside
[AIM_MIN_ALT_FT, AIM_MAX_ALT_FT].
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-8

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-02
TITLE: No alert before a valid target exists
STATEMENT: >>>
Before any valid selected altitude has ever been received,
selected_altitude_valid shall be false and no alert shall be asserted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-8

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-03
TITLE: Invalid altitude forces CRUISE
STATEMENT: >>>
When the current altitude is invalid, the alerter shall force state to
CRUISE and shall clear deviation_since_ms and both alert flags.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-6

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-04
TITLE: CRUISE to APPROACHING
STATEMENT: >>>
From CRUISE, the alerter shall transition to APPROACHING when
|altitude - selected| <= AIM_APPROACH_BAND_FT.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-6

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-05
TITLE: APPROACHING transitions
STATEMENT: >>>
From APPROACHING, the alerter shall transition to CAPTURED when
|altitude - selected| <= AIM_CAPTURE_BAND_FT, and shall transition back to
CRUISE when |altitude - selected| > AIM_APPROACH_BAND_FT + AIM_HYSTERESIS_FT.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-6

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-06
TITLE: CAPTURED to DEVIATION
STATEMENT: >>>
From CAPTURED, when |altitude - selected| > AIM_DEVIATION_BAND_FT
continuously for >= AIM_DEVIATION_PERSIST_MS and approach_mode is false, the
alerter shall transition to DEVIATION.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-7

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-07
TITLE: Deviation timer reset
STATEMENT: >>>
From CAPTURED, the deviation timer (deviation_since_ms) shall reset to zero
whenever |altitude - selected| <= AIM_DEVIATION_BAND_FT.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-7

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-08
TITLE: DEVIATION to CAPTURED
STATEMENT: >>>
From DEVIATION, the alerter shall transition back to CAPTURED when
|altitude - selected| <= AIM_DEVIATION_BAND_FT - AIM_HYSTERESIS_FT.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-7

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-09
TITLE: Approach mode inhibits deviation
STATEMENT: >>>
While approach_mode is true, the alerter shall never report state DEVIATION
or alert_deviation=true. If already in DEVIATION when approach_mode becomes
true, it shall revert immediately to CAPTURED and restart the deviation
timer from the current call's now_ms.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-7

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-ALT-10
TITLE: Alert flags follow state exactly
STATEMENT: >>>
alert_approaching shall be true if and only if state == APPROACHING;
alert_deviation shall be true if and only if state == DEVIATION.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-6

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-MON-01
TITLE: Good-sample criterion
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_monitor_update shall consider a channel "good" for a given call only when
its decoded word is valid and its SSM is NORMAL_OPERATION.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-MON-02
TITLE: Staleness detection
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_monitor_update shall record the time of the most recent good sample per
channel and shall set that channel's stale flag when more than
AIM_CHANNEL_STALE_MS has elapsed since the last good sample. A channel that
has never produced a good sample shall be reported invalid, not stale.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-MON-03
TITLE: Miscompare latch
STATEMENT: >>>
When both channels are good and not stale, aim_monitor_update shall compute
|ch1.altitude_ft - ch2.altitude_ft| and shall latch a miscompare when that
difference exceeds AIM_MISCOMPARE_THRESHOLD_FT continuously for
>= AIM_MISCOMPARE_PERSIST_MS.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-MON-04
TITLE: Miscompare clear
STATEMENT: >>>
Once latched, the miscompare flag shall clear only when the difference stays
<= AIM_MISCOMPARE_THRESHOLD_FT continuously for >= AIM_MISCOMPARE_PERSIST_MS.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-MON-05
TITLE: Frozen timers when a channel is unusable
STATEMENT: >>>
When either channel is not usable (invalid or stale), the divergence and
convergence timers shall be frozen: neither advanced nor reset.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-MON-06
TITLE: Altitude reconciliation and fail-over
STATEMENT: >>>
aim_monitor_update shall output a reconciled altitude from ch1 (primary) when
usable, else from ch2 when usable, else shall report altitude_available=false.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TIM-01
TITLE: Time is caller-supplied
STATEMENT: >>>
All persistence and staleness computations shall be based solely on the
caller-supplied now_ms parameter (elapsed-time arithmetic using unsigned
32-bit wraparound-safe subtraction), and shall not depend on wall-clock time
or any internal call counter.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-9

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TIM-02
TITLE: No hidden I/O or allocation
STATEMENT: >>>
The core library shall perform no blocking calls, dynamic memory allocation,
or hardware I/O; aim_step shall be callable at any rate and shall produce a
result based only on its inputs and prior state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-9
